WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.220
Does gun control actually
stop gun violence?

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.269
So first, let's point
out a quick statistic.

00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:07.560
Violence statistics-- not
just gun violence statistics,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.960
violence statistics matter.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.390
It is true that if have an
armed population, in many cases

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.270
you have a more
polite population.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.539
According to PolitiFact,
which is a far-left source,

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:19.580
for England and Wales,
the rate of violent crimes

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.020
is 775 per 100,000 people.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.230
For the United States, that
rate is 383 violent crimes

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.830
per 100,000 people.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.490
The UK has double the violent
crime rate of the United States

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.960
according to PolitiFact.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.326
And they have virtually
no guns in their society.

00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:34.950
How about gun control
in other nations?

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.900
What you would expect is, again,
this one to one correlation.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.520
Because people keep
suggesting over, and over,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.240
and over, more guns
means more crime.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:40.740
OK.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.930
Let's look at the
European countries.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.790
Let's take the United
States completely out of it.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.140
OK.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.350
The gun homicide rate in the
United States, first of all,

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.220
has declined faster
than Australia's did it

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.940
after its gun buyback
and ban program.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.470
And it's hard to
measure the impact

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.080
on mass shootings of
Australia's gun buyback program,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.620
because there were so few
mass shootings before that.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.460
But if you look at gun
control in other nations,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.080
right, the Small
Arms Survey of 2007

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.690
estimates civilian ownership
of firearms by nation.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.720
The United States ranked
by far at the top.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.230
We have 101 guns
per 100 residents.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.260
Number eight is
Norway and Norway

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.420
has 31 guns per 100 residents.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.590
France is ninth.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.030
The UK ranks 82nd.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.520
So the UK doesn't have
virtually any guns.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.800
Norway has a lot more guns.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.150
And yet Norway is
near the bottom

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.070
of the list in terms
of homicide rate,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.670
just 0.56 murders per
100,000 inhabitants.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:32.056
In France ranks somewhere
near the middle of the pack.

00:01:32.056 --> 00:01:33.930
They have triple the
homicide rate of Norway,

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.340
but they have way fewer guns.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.400
Which suggests that maybe this
has very little to do with guns

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.419
and it has a lot more to
do with the population that

00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:42.210
is in your country.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.910
And you see this in
the United States too.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.440
There's no
correlation whatsoever

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.450
between a state having
a high firearm ownership

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.580
rate and a high crime rate.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.670
So the 10 lowest
homicide jurisdictions

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.024
in the United States are New
Hampshire, Vermont, Iowa,

00:01:55.024 --> 00:01:56.940
Massachusetts, Utah,
Minnesota, Maine, Hawaii,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:57.990
Idaho, and Wyoming.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.420
Six of those 10 states
earn a D or an F

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.535
from the Brady Campaign
on gun control.

00:02:02.535 --> 00:02:04.890
I mean, if you go to
Vermont or New Hampshire,

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.605
everybody has a gun and
there's no gun violence.

00:02:07.605 --> 00:02:09.479
And the reason for that
is because the people

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:11.892
in Vermont and New Hampshire
are not shooting each other.

00:02:11.892 --> 00:02:13.800
And this is really not
all that difficult.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.510
And when you look at the
other end of the spectrum,

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.790
when you look at the states
that do have high rates of gun

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.230
violence, there are a
bunch of states, actually,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.460
they have a lot of gun control.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.918
And, of course, everybody in
the Second Amendment community

00:02:22.918 --> 00:02:26.630
is familiar with localities like
Washington D.C. and Chicago.

